  "independent_findings": [
    "Current printed HNT224 hero-hit WHEN earns one independent layer at hit; its Mark effect occurs only on resolution. Existing Mark removal within the hit event remains unchanged. Proposal adds exactly this one Red identity to the existing shared simple-hit spec using a non-token MARK primitive.",
    "Full actual damage -> OnHit -> WTRHit path reaches the common producer before generic Hit. Existing spec-based skip now suppresses the old canonical/compiled inline selected Hit, avoiding double Mark. Positive amount/live controller/no-abilities/hit-suppression/Hero-target/actual Hero seat+UID gates apply at earn, not on later physical source state.",
    "Captured layer stores actual controller separately from physical source owner, source UID and original hit hero UID/seat plus return Damage/combat context. Nothing marks during queueing. Empty token string remains isset for the actual existing dispatch; explicit MARK discriminator and static mapped spec prevent entering token creation.",
    "Deferred resolver checks live captured controller/recipient and original current Hero identity, rejecting a different replacement Hero UID or wrong zone/seat. It does not consult current attackTarget, the physical source, its later CardID/controller/abilities/suppression, so an earned layer is not cancelled or redirected by those changes. Same Hero physical identity with a transformed face remains valid; this is not a general incarnation/security audit.",
    "All original15 token rows are exact, their nonempty payload values are unchanged under null-coalescing, and the entire token resolution branch/helper/global-controller restoration body is raw identical. CnC, ordinary activated payment/resolver functions and every byte outside six declared anchors are preserved. No GL/ROS/Core/canonical/generated/emitter/held094 manager changes.",
    "Existing generic ability resolution calls the synchronous primitive then restores captured Damage/combatStep and turnplayer priority. Its legacy remove-before-call behavior is untouched; the selected Mark helper has no await, queue or source-dependent continuation, so this change does not claim or bypass the denied generic ROS completion repair. No AP/resource/GA cost or refund is introduced.",
    "Actual current0942 includes only the separately applied141 WTRCards/Boltyn changes relative to prior333; all70 actual guards are verified and WTRAbilities remains original f33a before application. Historical native333/source evidence is not relabeled as a current0942 run. Read-only candidate projection9fbaa is validated but inactive."
  ],
